  },
  {
   "post_type": "answer",
   "post_id": 64246483,
   "parent_id": 64246400,
   "author_user_id": 1687119,
   "author_display_name": "dbush",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": false,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/a/64246483",
   "score": 2,
   "created_utc": "2020-10-07T14:40:51Z",
   "last_edit_utc": null,
   "last_activity_utc": "2020-10-07T14:40:51Z",
   "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
   "body_html": "<p>You can only pass to <code>free</code> a pointer that was returned from <code>malloc</code>, <code>realloc</code>, or <code>calloc</code>.</p>\n<p>If you want to remove a value from the middle of any array (dynamically allocated or otherwise), you need to move each value above it down by one element.  You'll also want to keep track of how many &quot;active&quot; elements the array contains in some way.</p>\n"
  },
  {
